Linux software flowtable integration for RTL8197F / OpenWrt 24.10.

Explicit activation: rtl8197f-accel software on
Status/check: rtl8197f-accel status; rtl8197f-accel verify
Return to normal per-packet forwarding: rtl8197f-accel software off

This is Linux nf_flow_table under firewall4/conntrack ownership, not the
proprietary Realtek cache. Hardware NAT remains unavailable. Established
offloaded traffic does not traverse every regular forward hook. Use strict
mode for per-packet logging/filtering and configurations requiring SQM.

The dependency kmod-nft-offload requires the OpenWrt IPv6 feature. Installing
this package does not turn on WAN IPv6 or change IPv6 firewall rules. Check
the actual built image size; small-flash profiles do not include it by default.
Permanent MW5 software activation is locked pending stress validation. Repair missing
WAN connectivity before enabling it on RD05. Cudy profiles remain UART-only.

MW5: rtl8197f-accel test software 120 permits a volatile, bounded experiment.
Permanent MW5 activation and Realtek hardware NAT remain blocked.
See target/linux/realtek/rtl8197f/ACCELERATION.md for prerequisites and rollback.
